„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoAnd when the Pharisees saw it, they said unto his disciples, Why eateth your Master with publicans and sinners?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙnBut when Jesus heard that, he said unto them, They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙBut go ye and learn what that meaneth, I will have mercy, and not sacrifice: for I am not come to call the righteous, but sinners to repentance.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙqThen came to him the disciples of John, saying, Why do we and the Pharisees fast oft, but thy disciples fast not?¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÍAnd Jesus said unto them, Can the children of the bridechamber mourn, as long as the bridegroom is with them? but the days will come, when the bridegroom shall be taken from them, and then shall they fast.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ”No man putteth a piece of new cloth unto an old garment, for that which is put in to fill it up taketh from the garment, and the rent is made worse.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·Neither do men put new wine into old bottles: else the bottles break, and the wine runneth out, and the bottles perish: but they put new wine into new bottles, and both are preserved.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses™„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼While he spake these things unto them, behold, there came a certain ruler, and worshipped him, saying, My daughter is even now dead: but come and lay thy hand upon her, and she shall live.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ<And Jesus arose, and followed him, and so did his disciples.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ‚And, behold, a woman, which was diseased with an issue of blood twelve years, came behind him, and touched the hem of his garment:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNfor she said within herself, If I may but touch his garment, I shall be whole.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¤But Jesus turned him about, and when he saw her, he said, Daughter, be of good comfort; thy faith hath made thee whole. And the woman was made whole from that hour.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ`And when Jesus came into the ruler's house, and saw the minstrels and the people making a noise,¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙehe said unto them, Give place: for the maid is not dead, but sleepeth. And they laughed him to scorn.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]But when the people were put forth, he went in, and took her by the hand, and the maid arose.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ3And the fame hereof went abroad into all that land.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter	«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtAnd when Jesus departed thence, two blind men followed him, crying, and saying, Thou Son of David, have mercy on us.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙŸAnd when he was come into the house, the blind men came to him: and Jesus saith unto them, Believe ye that I am able to do this? They said unto him, Yea, Lord.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙKThen touched he their eyes, saying, According to your faith be it unto you.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ]And their eyes were opened; and Jesus straitly charged them, saying, See that no man know it.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙNBut they, when they were departed, spread abroad his fame in all that country.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book'§chapter	«first_verse ªlast_verse"¦verses“„¥verse ¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙPAs they went out, behold, they brought to him a dumb man possessed with a devil.¦layout ªlast_verse „¥verse!¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙvAnd when the devil was cast out, the dumb spake: and the multitudes marvelled, saying, It was never so seen in Israel.¦layout ªlast_verse!„¥verse"¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙOBut the Pharisees said, He casteth out devils through the prince of the devils.¦layout ªlast_verse"…¤book'§chapter	«first_verse#ªlast_verse&¦verses”„¥verse#¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ·And Jesus went about all the cities and villages, teaching in their synagogues, and preaching the gospel of the kingdom, and healing every sickness and every disease among the people.¦layout ªlast_verse#„¥verse$¯paragraph_startÃ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ“But when he saw the multitudes, he was moved with compassion on them, because they fainted, and were scattered abroad, as sheep having no shepherd.¦layout ªlast_verse$„¥verse%¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ\Then saith he unto his disciples, The harvest truly is plenteous, but the labourers are few;¦layout ªlast_verse%„¥verse&¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ^Pray ye therefore the Lord of the harvest, that he will send forth labourers into his harvest.¦layout ªlast_verse&